{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"3573b22b63d13a3f","type":"text","text":"▶ Start\njourney-builder.opened","x":0,"y":0,"width":160,"height":80,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"778b7a9feb3ae19b","type":"group","label":"Open Journey Builder via command","x":200,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b028fccd1b2bf2d2","type":"text","text":"Opens the Journey Builder via the command palette. Verifies the sidebar appears, then closes it to prepare for the ribbon test.\n8 actions","x":250,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"eb01826c3f8dee85","type":"group","label":"Open Journey Builder via ribbon","x":720,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"fe47e944bc15f974","type":"text","text":"Clicks the Journey Builder ribbon button. Sidebar opens on the right with welcome screen showing Create New and Open Existing cards.\n9 actions","x":770,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"096914598c56b90e","type":"group","label":"Create a new journey via setup form","x":1240,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"4328194db1061b26","type":"text","text":"Clicks Create New Journey to open the setup form. Fills in the journey name, description, and start event, then verifies the form is complete.\n18 actions","x":1290,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"465b7de4d44be1e2","type":"group","label":"Add a step to the journey","x":1760,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"e060c994fc1ef450","type":"text","text":"Clicks Continue to enter the step editor. Sees an empty state, then adds the first step, enters a title, and sets the journey end event. The JSON preview toggle and action list become visible.\n19 actions","x":1810,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"5869ae221831e394","type":"group","label":"Export journey JSON","x":2280,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"0afadd6ac98b4ae6","type":"text","text":"Clicks the Export button to save the journey as a JSON file in the vault. Verifies the file was written successfully via the event trace.\n9 actions","x":2330,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"d5e1b2d0ddda393d","type":"group","label":"Navigate and edit steps with prev/next","x":2800,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"a46bd2f663553621","type":"text","text":"Edits the step description, adds a second step, and uses prev/next navigation to move between them. Verifies the step counter updates correctly at each navigation point.\n21 actions","x":2850,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"cbf724aed1ec0a58","type":"group","label":"Add actions to a step","x":3320,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"8fed78830670436c","type":"text","text":"Opens the tool picker to add actions to a step. Selects a tool, fills in its fields, adds more actions, reorders them with up/down, removes one, and verifies the action count updates.\n53 actions","x":3370,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"48af19f60d8e41bd","type":"group","label":"Live JSON preview panel","x":3840,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"91dad1fe29eda790","type":"text","text":"Toggles the JSON preview panel at the bottom of the sidebar. Verifies the panel shows valid, formatted JSON that reflects the current journey definition. Tests copy-to-clipboard, then makes an edit and confirms the JSON updates live.\n15 actions","x":3890,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"eb59e46e6051a567","type":"group","label":"Event autocomplete and command picker","x":4360,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"846a3c80c718f267","type":"text","text":"Tests the smart input features: typing a partial event name shows an autocomplete dropdown, command actions get a command picker, and assert actions get a guided type-specific form.\n28 actions","x":4410,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"813dbf39e7abcd81","type":"group","label":"Canvas sync — real-time canvas generation","x":4880,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"e744f97de917c09a","type":"text","text":"Verifies that a companion canvas file is generated in real-time as the journey is built. The canvas shows a left-to-right flow with start/end nodes and step groups. Changes to steps and metadata are reflected automatically.\n10 actions","x":4930,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"03b9858c69750735","type":"group","label":"Full export — JSON, test file, and canvas","x":5400,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"0d5d086787321162","type":"text","text":"Exports the complete journey as three files: a .journey.json with the full definition, a .test.ts executor wrapper, and a .canvas companion file. Verifies all three files are created in the vault.\n12 actions","x":5450,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"cb4b9b046092816c","type":"group","label":"Open existing journey for editing","x":5920,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"3a9f2abe133c93e0","type":"text","text":"Closes the current journey, returns to the welcome screen, and uses 'Open Existing' to load the previously exported journey back into the step editor. Verifies all fields are populated and the companion canvas opens alongside.\n16 actions","x":5970,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"9f5182de48daf2e7","type":"group","label":"Preview run with live canvas feedback","x":6440,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":160},
		{"id":"6d36d0b2ae948a7c","type":"text","text":"Runs a preview of the journey inside Obsidian. Steps execute one by one, and the companion canvas updates live — step nodes turn green (pass) or red (fail). Screenshots are captured and embedded in step groups.\n14 actions","x":6490,"y":10,"width":380,"height":60},
		{"id":"8b1c68c61b1384aa","type":"text","text":"⏹ End","x":6960,"y":0,"width":160,"height":80,"color":"1"}
	],
